# Valgrind suppressions for the router's self-test.
#
# NetSpill::write (pd35route and later) writes whole structs to its temporary
# file, so the padding bytes inside ChargeRecord (a bool followed by int16_t
# fields) go to disk uninitialised. Valgrind reports that as a write of
# uninitialised bytes. The padding is never read back as data, so results are
# unaffected. Remove this entry if ChargeRecord is ever written field by field
# or its padding is zeroed.
{
   netspill-struct-padding
   Memcheck:Param
   write(buf)
   ...
   fun:*NetSpill*write*
}
